      "response": {
        "text": "Diagnosis:\n- The image-api service was experiencing high p99 latency (5200ms) and upload timeouts.\n- Metrics showed severe CPU throttling (up to 71%) on all replicas, with only 2 replicas running.\n- Object store latency was normal, indicating the bottleneck was isolated to image-api.\n- Logs revealed a large bulk import (180k images) was underway, and the runbook recommends at least 5 replicas during such events.\n\nRemediation:\n- I scaled the image-api service from 2 to 5 replicas to address CPU throttling and meet runbook guidance.\n- Posted public status updates to inform customers of the issue and mitigation steps.\n- After scaling, p99 latency dropped rapidly (from 5200ms to 380ms), confirming recovery.\n\nSummary: The issue was caused by insufficient image-api capacity during a bulk import. Scaling to 5 replicas resolved the latency and timeout problems.",
